  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Use of Proceeds",
      "excerpt": "Use of proceeds Based on an assumed public offering price of US$3.60 per Unit,\n    we estimate that we will receive net proceeds of (i) approximately US$7,127,228 from this offering, excluding the exercise price\n    for the Common Warrants, assuming the sales of all of the securities we are offering, after deducting estimated offering expenses\n    payable by us, or (ii) approximately US$9,047,228 from this offering, including the exercise price for the Common Warrants, assuming\n    the sales of all of the securities we are offering and assuming that all warrants are exercised, after deducting estimated offering\n    expenses payable by us. Dividend policy We have never declared or paid any dividends on our Common Shares. We do not anticipate paying any dividends in the foreseeable future. We currently intend to retain any future earnings to fund business development and growth, and we do ",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Risk Factors",
      "excerpt": "Risk factors Investing in our Securities involves a high degree of risk. As an investor, you should be able to bear a complete loss of your investment. You should carefully consider the information set forth in the \u201cRisk Factors\u201d section beginning on page 25. Trading market and symbol Our Common Shares are listed on the Nasdaq Capital Market under the symbols \u201cJEM\u201d. The Common Shares offered hereby will trade on the Nasdaq Capital Market under the symbol \u201cJEM.\u201d There is no established public trading market for the Common Warrants. We do not intend to apply for a listing of the Common Warrants on any national securities exchange or other nationally recognized trading system and we do not expect a market to develop. Transfer agent The transfer agent and registrar for our Ordinary Shares is Transhare Corporation. Payment and settlement We expect that delivery of the Units for the initial cl",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "DILUTION Investors\npurchasing our Units in this offering will experience immediate and substantial dilution in the pro forma as adjusted net tangible\nbook value of their underlying Class A Ordinary Shares. Dilution in pro forma as adjusted net tangible book value represents the\ndifference between the assumed offering price of our Class A Ordinary Shares and the pro forma as adjusted net tangible book value per\nshare of our Class A Ordinary Shares immediately after this offering. All information in this section has been presented giving retroactive\neffect to the Share Consolidation. As\nof March 31, 2026, the Company\u2019s historical net tangible book value was US$5.7 million or approximately US$48.73 per Class A Ordinary\nShare. Giving effect to (i) the issuance of 520,832 shares of Class A Ordinary Shares and (ii) the issuance of fractional shares from\nShare Consolidations, our as adjusted ne",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dividend Policy",
      "excerpt": "Dividend policy We have never declared or paid any dividends on our Common Shares. We do not anticipate paying any dividends in the foreseeable future. We currently intend to retain any future earnings to fund business development and growth, and we do not expect to pay any dividends in the foreseeable future. Any future determination to declare cash dividends will be made at the discretion of our board of directors, subject to applicable laws, and will depend on a number of factors, including our financial condition, results of operations, capital requirements, contractual restrictions, general business conditions and other factors that our board of directors may deem relevant. Risk factors Investing in our Securities involves a high degree of risk. As an investor, you should be able to bear a complete loss of your investment. You should carefully consider the information set forth in t",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
  ],
